<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>K2 Line Watch</name><Style id="sub"><IconStyle><color>ff6b13c4</color><scale>1.1</scale></IconStyle></Style><Style id="area"><LineStyle><color>ff6b13c4</color><width>1</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>336b13c4</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="line"><LineStyle><color>ff1b211d</color><width>2</width></LineStyle></Style><Folder><name>End substations</name><Placemark><name>Hillje Substation (CenterPoint; new 765 kV yard at existing 345 kV site)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: hillje-blu-lacy<br>project: Hillje to Blu Lacy<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Hillje Substation (CenterPoint; new 765 kV yard at existing 345 kV site)<br>county: TX: Wharton<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Existing Hillje 345 kV substation at 10973 CR 403 (29.029634, -96.235950) per CenterPoint's Docket 51568 notice. The new 765 kV substation is planned next to it, and the route links on the Hillje-Blu Lacy map end within about 1 mile of this point.<br>source: https://www.centerpointenergy.com/en-us/Corp/Documents/Space-City/Attachment-6.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-96.236,29.0296</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Blu Lacy Substation (AEP Texas, proposed)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: hillje-blu-lacy<br>project: Hillje to Blu Lacy<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Blu Lacy Substation (AEP Texas, proposed)<br>county: TX: Nueces<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Read from where the route links meet on two AEP route maps (Hillje-Blu Lacy and Blu Lacy-Howard), each georeferenced to known towns; both put it about 2 mi west of US 77 between Driscoll and Bishop. Uncertainty about 2-3 mi.<br>source: https://www.aeptransmission.com/texas/hillje-blulacy/docs/AEP_H-BL_Map.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-97.82,27.65</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Blu Lacy Substation (AEP Texas, proposed)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: blu-lacy-howard<br>project: Blu Lacy to Howard<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Blu Lacy Substation (AEP Texas, proposed)<br>county: TX: Nueces<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Read from where the route links meet on two AEP route maps (Hillje-Blu Lacy and Blu Lacy-Howard), each georeferenced to known towns; both put it about 2 mi west of US 77 between Driscoll and Bishop. Uncertainty about 2-3 mi.<br>source: https://www.aeptransmission.com/texas/hillje-blulacy/docs/AEP_H-BL_Map.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-97.82,27.65</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Howard (Howard Road) Substation (CPS Energy)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: blu-lacy-howard<br>project: Blu Lacy to Howard<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Howard (Howard Road) Substation (CPS Energy)<br>county: TX: Bexar<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: PUC Docket 59336 order says the existing Howard 345 kV station is about 2 mi north of the SH 1604 / SH 16 intersection (2024 Docket 57115 notice says about 3 mi northeast). Point is placed between the two readings, using that intersection geocoded from OpenStreetMap (29.2335, -98.5843).<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/59336_95_1597112.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-98.567,29.263</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Dinosaur Switch (Oncor, proposed; ERCOT 'New Substation 2')</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: dinosaur-watermill<br>project: Dinosaur to Watermill<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Dinosaur Switch (Oncor, proposed; ERCOT 'New Substation 2')<br>county: TX: Somervell<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Oncor says it is about 3 mi north of the City of Glen Rose. The point is Glen Rose (OSM 32.2341, -97.7550) moved 3 mi north.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/dinosaur-to-longshore-765-kv-transmission-line-project.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-97.755,32.2776</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Watermill Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: dinosaur-watermill<br>project: Dinosaur to Watermill<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Watermill Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Dallas<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: PUC Docket 57918 order says Watermill switch is about 3.5 mi west of the IH-45 / Malloy Bridge Rd intersection. The point is that intersection (OSM 32.5612, -96.6643) moved 3.5 mi west. It lands on Watermill Rd, which fits.<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/57918_22_1510937.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-96.7245,32.5612</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Watermill Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: watermill-martin-lake<br>project: Watermill to Martin Lake<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Watermill Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Dallas<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: PUC Docket 57918 order says Watermill switch is about 3.5 mi west of the IH-45 / Malloy Bridge Rd intersection. The point is that intersection (OSM 32.5612, -96.6643) moved 3.5 mi west. It lands on Watermill Rd, which fits.<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/57918_22_1510937.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-96.7245,32.5612</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Martin Lake (Oncor 765 kV switchyard at existing Martin Lake 345 kV substation)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: watermill-martin-lake<br>project: Watermill to Martin Lake<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Martin Lake (Oncor 765 kV switchyard at existing Martin Lake 345 kV substation)<br>county: TX: Rusk<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Centroid of the Martin Lake Power Plant in OpenStreetMap (Nominatim), near Tatum. ERCOT plans the new 765 kV switchyard at the existing Martin Lake 345 kV substation at the plant, so the yard itself may sit 1-2 mi from this point.<br>source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/search?query=Martin%20Lake%20Power%20Plant]]></description><Point><coordinates>-94.5741,32.2583</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Martin Lake (Oncor 765 kV switchyard at existing Martin Lake 345 kV substation)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: martin-lake-hillje<br>project: Martin Lake to Hillje<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Martin Lake (Oncor 765 kV switchyard at existing Martin Lake 345 kV substation)<br>county: TX: Rusk<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Centroid of the Martin Lake Power Plant in OpenStreetMap (Nominatim), near Tatum. ERCOT plans the new 765 kV switchyard at the existing Martin Lake 345 kV substation at the plant, so the yard itself may sit 1-2 mi from this point.<br>source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/search?query=Martin%20Lake%20Power%20Plant]]></description><Point><coordinates>-94.5741,32.2583</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hillje Substation (CenterPoint; new 765 kV yard at existing 345 kV site)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: martin-lake-hillje<br>project: Martin Lake to Hillje<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Hillje Substation (CenterPoint; new 765 kV yard at existing 345 kV site)<br>county: TX: Wharton<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Existing Hillje 345 kV substation at 10973 CR 403 (29.029634, -96.235950) per CenterPoint's Docket 51568 notice. The new 765 kV substation is planned next to it, and the route links on the Hillje-Blu Lacy map end within about 1 mile of this point.<br>source: https://www.centerpointenergy.com/en-us/Corp/Documents/Space-City/Attachment-6.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-96.236,29.0296</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Howard (Howard Road) Substation (CPS Energy)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: howard-bell-east<br>project: Howard to Bell County East<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Howard (Howard Road) Substation (CPS Energy)<br>county: TX: Bexar<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: PUC Docket 59336 order says the existing Howard 345 kV station is about 2 mi north of the SH 1604 / SH 16 intersection (2024 Docket 57115 notice says about 3 mi northeast). Point is placed between the two readings, using that intersection geocoded from OpenStreetMap (29.2335, -98.5843).<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/59336_95_1597112.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-98.567,29.263</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bell County East Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: howard-bell-east<br>project: Howard to Bell County East<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Bell County East Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Bell<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Oncor says it is 5.5 mi southeast of the City of Temple. The point is Temple (OSM 31.0984, -97.3430) moved 5.5 mi southeast.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/bell-county-east---big-hill-765-kv-transmission-line-project.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-97.2772,31.042</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bell County East Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: bell-east-watermill<br>project: Bell County East to Watermill<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Bell County East Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Bell<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Oncor says it is 5.5 mi southeast of the City of Temple. The point is Temple (OSM 31.0984, -97.3430) moved 5.5 mi southeast.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/bell-county-east---big-hill-765-kv-transmission-line-project.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-97.2772,31.042</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Watermill Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: bell-east-watermill<br>project: Bell County East to Watermill<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Watermill Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Dallas<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: PUC Docket 57918 order says Watermill switch is about 3.5 mi west of the IH-45 / Malloy Bridge Rd intersection. The point is that intersection (OSM 32.5612, -96.6643) moved 3.5 mi west. It lands on Watermill Rd, which fits.<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/57918_22_1510937.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-96.7245,32.5612</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Euclid Substation (LCRA TSC; new 765 kV yard next to existing Euclid 345 kV station)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: euclid-765<br>project: Euclid 765 kV substation and line<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Euclid Substation (LCRA TSC; new 765 kV yard next to existing Euclid 345 kV station)<br>county: TX: Caldwell<br>location_quality: county<br>how_placed: Point read off the low-resolution ERCOT/LCRA 26RPG001 project map (georeferenced to other STEP substations; uncertainty about 5 mi). The county is from ERCOT's project county list (Caldwell, Colorado, Gonzales, Lavaca, Wharton). Euclid sits on the John Dumas-Hornsby 345 kV line about 2 mi from Misty substation; no exact site has been published.<br>source: https://www.ercot.com/files/docs/2026/03/16/13.-26RPG001-LCRA-TSC-and-CEHE-Euclid-765-kV-Substation-and-Transmission-Line-Addition-Project_final.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-97.781,29.945</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hillje Substation (CenterPoint; new 765 kV yard at existing 345 kV site)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: euclid-765<br>project: Euclid 765 kV substation and line<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Hillje Substation (CenterPoint; new 765 kV yard at existing 345 kV site)<br>county: TX: Wharton<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Existing Hillje 345 kV substation at 10973 CR 403 (29.029634, -96.235950) per CenterPoint's Docket 51568 notice. The new 765 kV substation is planned next to it, and the route links on the Hillje-Blu Lacy map end within about 1 mile of this point.<br>source: https://www.centerpointenergy.com/en-us/Corp/Documents/Space-City/Attachment-6.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-96.236,29.0296</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bell County East Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: bell-east-big-hill<br>project: Bell County East to Big Hill<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: Bell County East Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Bell<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: CCN notice: Link A0 starts at the 765 kV switchyard 'approximately 2,960 feet southeast from the intersection of Stallion Rd and Shaw Ln'; intersection located in OSM (Nominatim road segments meet at 31.0119,-97.2595; OSM names it Shaw Road) and offset 0.56 mi SE. Near Heidenheimer, SE of Temple.<br>source: https://texasscorecard.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Bell-East-Application-Notice.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-97.2528,31.0062</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Big Hill Substation (LCRA TSC; new 765 kV yard adjacent to existing 345 kV)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: bell-east-big-hill<br>project: Bell County East to Big Hill<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: Big Hill Substation (LCRA TSC; new 765 kV yard adjacent to existing 345 kV)<br>county: TX: Schleicher<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: HIFLD substation layer point named BIG HILL (345 kV, Schleicher Co.); matches utility description '13 miles northeast of Eldorado' (computed 13.3 mi NNE). New 765 kV yard will be adjacent.<br>source: https://services5.arcgis.com/HDRa0B57OVrv2E1q/ArcGIS/rest/services/Electric_Substations/FeatureServer/0]]></description><Point><coordinates>-100.5431,31.0472</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Big Hill Substation (LCRA TSC; new 765 kV yard adjacent to existing 345 kV)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: big-hill-sand-lake<br>project: Big Hill to Sand Lake<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: Big Hill Substation (LCRA TSC; new 765 kV yard adjacent to existing 345 kV)<br>county: TX: Schleicher<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: HIFLD substation layer point named BIG HILL (345 kV, Schleicher Co.); matches utility description '13 miles northeast of Eldorado' (computed 13.3 mi NNE). New 765 kV yard will be adjacent.<br>source: https://services5.arcgis.com/HDRa0B57OVrv2E1q/ArcGIS/rest/services/Electric_Substations/FeatureServer/0]]></description><Point><coordinates>-100.5431,31.0472</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sand Lake Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: big-hill-sand-lake<br>project: Big Hill to Sand Lake<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: Sand Lake Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Ward<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: PUC order (Docket 57633) and Oncor: 'in Ward County, approximately six miles northeast of Pecos', on the NW side of an FM road; computed 6 mi NE offset from Pecos city center (31.4254,-103.4953).<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/57633_48_1526524.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-103.423,31.487</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Howard (Howard Road) Station (CPS Energy)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: howard-solstice<br>project: Howard to Solstice<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 6<br>window: Late<br>substation: Howard (Howard Road) Station (CPS Energy)<br>county: TX: Bexar<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: HIFLD substation layer point named HOWARD (Bexar Co.); CCN letter puts the existing Howard 345 kV station about 2 mi north of the SH 1604 / SH 16 intersection (this point is ~3 mi north of it). The 765 kV yard will be in the vicinity.<br>source: https://www.cpsenergy.com/content/dam/corporate/en/Documents/Infrastructure/howard-solstice/howard-solstice-transmission-project/part-2-update-files/Utilities-Letter-and-List-ada-31726.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-98.5723,29.2806</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Solstice Substation (AEP Texas)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: howard-solstice<br>project: Howard to Solstice<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 6<br>window: Late<br>substation: Solstice Substation (AEP Texas)<br>county: TX: Pecos<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: HIFLD substation layer point named SOLSTICE (345 kV, Pecos Co.); matches '28 miles west of Fort Stockton along I-10' (computed 28.4 mi W).<br>source: https://www.cpsenergy.com/content/dam/corporate/en/Documents/Infrastructure/howard-solstice/howard-solstice-transmission-project/part-2-update-files/Utilities-Letter-and-List-ada-31726.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-103.3628,30.9484</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Dinosaur Switch (Oncor, proposed)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: dinosaur-longshore<br>project: Dinosaur to Longshore<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 6<br>window: Late<br>substation: Dinosaur Switch (Oncor, proposed)<br>county: TX: Somervell<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Two published descriptions agree: '3 miles north of Glen Rose' (offset from Glen Rose, 32.234,-97.755) and 'about 2 miles southeast of the existing Comanche Peak Switch' (HIFLD 32.298,-97.790).<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/59315_5651_1648107.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-97.762,32.278</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Longshore Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: dinosaur-longshore<br>project: Dinosaur to Longshore<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 6<br>window: Late<br>substation: Longshore Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Howard<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: Unnamed HIFLD 345 kV substation point that is the only 345 kV site matching '4.5 miles west of Forsan' (computed 5.0 mi W); OSM reverse-geocode places it on Longshore Road.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/dinosaur-to-longshore-765-kv-transmission-line-project.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-101.4523,32.1003</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Longshore Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: longshore-drill-hole<br>project: Longshore to Drill Hole<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 6<br>window: Late<br>substation: Longshore Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Howard<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: Unnamed HIFLD 345 kV substation point that is the only 345 kV site matching '4.5 miles west of Forsan' (computed 5.0 mi W); OSM reverse-geocode places it on Longshore Road.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/dinosaur-to-longshore-765-kv-transmission-line-project.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-101.4523,32.1003</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Drill Hole Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: longshore-drill-hole<br>project: Longshore to Drill Hole<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 6<br>window: Late<br>substation: Drill Hole Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Culberson<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: PUC order: 'in Culberson County near the Culberson and Reeves county line approximately six miles west of US 285 and approximately eight miles north of RM 652'; offsets computed from OSM geometry of US 285 and RM 652. Another Oncor page says 4 mi west of US 285, so expect error of up to ~3 mi.<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/59029_503_1678287.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-104.08,31.94</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>White Baker Substation (TNMP; new 345 kV yard at existing 138 kV station)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: white-baker-bottlebrush<br>project: White Baker to Bottlebrush<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: White Baker Substation (TNMP; new 345 kV yard at existing 138 kV station)<br>county: TX: Pecos<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: HIFLD substation layer point named WHITE BAKER (138 kV, Pecos Co.); matches '25-30 miles east of Fort Stockton on I-10' (computed 27 mi E). The 345 kV yard is being added at this existing station.<br>source: https://www.lcra.org/energy/electric-transmission/transmission-line-routing/bakersfield-to-white-baker-345-kv-transmission-line-project/]]></description><Point><coordinates>-102.4231,30.886</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bottlebrush Station (TNMP, proposed)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: white-baker-bottlebrush<br>project: White Baker to Bottlebrush<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: Bottlebrush Station (TNMP, proposed)<br>county: TX: Pecos<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: ERCOT/PUC Permian plan exhibit says the new Bottlebrush 345/138 kV substation is 'near the existing Century 138-kV station'; placed at HIFLD 'OXY CENTURY' point, which is ~2 mi NE of US 285 and ~25 mi SE of Fort Stockton, consistent with TNMP's 'about one mile northeast of US 285'. Exact site not published; expect error of a few miles.<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/57441_31_1469330.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-102.582,30.607</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bottlebrush Station (TNMP, proposed)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: bottlebrush-solstice<br>project: Bottlebrush to Solstice<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Bottlebrush Station (TNMP, proposed)<br>county: TX: Pecos<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: ERCOT/PUC Permian plan exhibit says the new Bottlebrush 345/138 kV substation is 'near the existing Century 138-kV station'; placed at HIFLD 'OXY CENTURY' point, which is ~2 mi NE of US 285 and ~25 mi SE of Fort Stockton, consistent with TNMP's 'about one mile northeast of US 285'. Exact site not published; expect error of a few miles.<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/57441_31_1469330.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-102.582,30.607</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Solstice Substation (AEP Texas)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: bottlebrush-solstice<br>project: Bottlebrush to Solstice<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Solstice Substation (AEP Texas)<br>county: TX: Pecos<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: HIFLD substation layer point named SOLSTICE (345 kV, Pecos Co.); matches '28 miles west of Fort Stockton along I-10' (computed 28.4 mi W).<br>source: https://www.cpsenergy.com/content/dam/corporate/en/Documents/Infrastructure/howard-solstice/howard-solstice-transmission-project/part-2-update-files/Utilities-Letter-and-List-ada-31726.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-103.3628,30.9484</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bakersfield Substation (LCRA TSC)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[projec