about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/Consavvy-to-Long-Creek-Switch-345kV.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-101.993,31.914</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Long Creek Switch</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: consavvy-long-creek<br>project: Consavvy to Long Creek<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: Long Creek Switch<br>county: TX: Shackelford<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Placed from Oncor notice map Fig. 12, georeferenced to the Jones/Shackelford county line and the OSM FM 604/SH 351 junction (Oncor text: 5.4 mi NE of that junction).<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/Consavvy-to-Long-Creek-Switch-345kV.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-99.54,32.63</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pine Substation</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: pine-mccloud<br>project: Pine to McCloud<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: Pine Substation<br>county: TX: El Paso<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: Project site says Pine is at the intersection of La Pine Ave and Appleton St (south of US 62/180); intersection geocoded from OSM street geometry.<br>source: https://pine-mccloudcentral.com/]]></description><Point><coordinates>-106.0812,31.8123</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>McCloud Central Substation</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: pine-mccloud<br>project: Pine to McCloud<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: McCloud Central Substation<br>county: TX: El Paso<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Project site says west of US 54 just south of the NM state line; notice map shows it about 0.8 mi west of US 54 at the state line, offset from the OSM US 54 crossing (~-106.333).<br>source: https://www.epelectric.com/el-paso-electric/uploads/PDFs/pine-mccloud-central_noticemap.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-106.347,31.995</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Tuskegee Substation</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: tuskegee-pine<br>project: Tuskegee to Pine<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: Tuskegee Substation<br>county: TX: El Paso<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Project site says east of Horizon City on Tuskegee Blvd between Indian Trail Dr and Little Lake Rd; OSM Tuskegee Ave/Indian Trail Dr junction (31.654,-106.063) plus constraints-map position just west of it.<br>source: https://tuskegee-pine.com/]]></description><Point><coordinates>-106.067,31.655</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pine Substation</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: tuskegee-pine<br>project: Tuskegee to Pine<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: Pine Substation<br>county: TX: El Paso<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: Project site says intersection of La Pine Ave and Appleton St; intersection geocoded from OSM street geometry.<br>source: https://tuskegee-pine.com/]]></description><Point><coordinates>-106.0812,31.8123</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rockhound Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: rockhound-longshore<br>project: Rockhound to Longshore (double circuit)<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Rockhound Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Midland<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Oncor: '2 miles southwest of the intersection of I-20 and FM 829 in Midland County'; the I-20/FM 829 junction is from OSM (~32.101,-101.865) and the point is offset 2 mi SW, just south of the Martin County line.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/longshore-to-rockhound-345-kv-transmission-line-project.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-101.889,32.08</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Longshore Switch (Oncor)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: rockhound-longshore<br>project: Rockhound to Longshore (double circuit)<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Longshore Switch (Oncor)<br>county: TX: Howard<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: Unnamed HIFLD 345 kV substation point that is the only 345 kV site matching '4.5 miles west of Forsan' (computed 5.0 mi W); OSM reverse-geocode places it on Longshore Road.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/dinosaur-to-longshore-765-kv-transmission-line-project.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-101.4523,32.1003</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CTT Gray Substation (existing 345 kV; new 765 kV)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: panhandle-plan<br>project: Panhandle Reliability Transmission Plan<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: CTT Gray Substation (existing 345 kV; new 765 kV)<br>county: TX: Gray<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: PUC Docket 37956 says Gray Substation is about 2 mi west-southwest of Lefors. The point is Lefors (OSM 35.4385, -100.8040) moved 2 mi WSW.<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/37956_9_649865.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-100.8369,35.4274</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CTT Celtic Green Substation (proposed 765/345 kV)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: panhandle-plan<br>project: Panhandle Reliability Transmission Plan<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: CTT Celtic Green Substation (proposed 765/345 kV)<br>county: TX: Wheeler<br>location_quality: county<br>how_placed: ERCOT says it will cut into the Gray-Tesla 345 kV line about 39 mi from Gray. The point is set about 38 mi ESE of Gray, the direction shown on CTT's Option 1 map. Expect 10+ mi error; Wheeler County is likely but not confirmed (Collingsworth or Donley are possible).<br>source: https://www.ercot.com/files/docs/2026/07/17/13.-EIR_Scope_Combined-AEPSC-Panhandle-Project-and-CTT-Panhandle-Reliability-Transmission-Plan-Project_RPG-July-2026.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-100.1895,35.2723</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CTT Cross Substation (existing 345 kV; new 765 kV)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: panhandle-plan<br>project: Panhandle Reliability Transmission Plan<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: CTT Cross Substation (existing 345 kV; new 765 kV)<br>county: TX: Hall<br>location_quality: town<br>how_placed: Placed at the town of Turkey: CTT labels this load site 'Cross/Turkey', and the georeferenced Option 1 map puts Cross near Turkey (about 10 mi uncertainty). Cross is on CTT's Silverton-Tesla 345 kV line, so Briscoe or Motley County cannot be ruled out.<br>source: https://www.ercot.com/files/docs/2026/07/20/12.-ERCOT-RPG_CTT-PH-Reliability-Transmission-Plan_Presentation_July_21_2026.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-100.8941,34.3939</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>ETT Tesla Substation (existing 345 kV)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: panhandle-plan<br>project: Panhandle Reliability Transmission Plan<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: ETT Tesla Substation (existing 345 kV)<br>county: TX: Childress<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: PUC Docket 37956 says Tesla is about 6 mi southeast of Childress. The point is Childress (OSM 34.4258, -100.2054) moved 6 mi southeast.<br>source: https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/37956_9_649865.PDF]]></description><Point><coordinates>-100.1309,34.3643</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Longshore Switch (Oncor, existing)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: panhandle-plan<br>project: Panhandle Reliability Transmission Plan<br>stage: 2<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Longshore Switch (Oncor, existing)<br>county: TX: Howard<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Oncor says it is about 4.5 mi west of the City of Forsan. The point is Forsan (OSM 32.1098, -101.3662) moved 4.5 mi west.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/dinosaur-to-longshore-765-kv-transmission-line-project.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-101.4432,32.1098</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Border Switch</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: border-clearfork<br>project: Border to Clearfork<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 6<br>window: Late<br>substation: Border Switch<br>county: TX: Loving<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Oncor: 7 mi SE of RM 652 &amp; CR 300 (OSM junction 31.972,-103.745, offset 7 mi SE) and ~6 mi south of the NM line; the two descriptions agree within ~1 mi.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/border-switch-clearfork-switch-345-kv-transmission-line-project.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-103.66,31.9</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Clearfork Switch</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: border-clearfork<br>project: Border to Clearfork<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 6<br>window: Late<br>substation: Clearfork Switch<br>county: TX: Andrews<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Oncor: 2 mi SW of SH 115 &amp; FM 181; junction taken from OSM (~32.182,-102.749) and offset 2 mi SW.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/border-switch-clearfork-switch-345-kv-transmission-line-project.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-102.773,32.161</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>El 