cription><Point><coordinates>-102.7775,32.165</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lamesa Switch</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: oncor-mascho-to-lamesa<br>project: Mascho to Lamesa<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 5<br>window: Act fast<br>substation: Lamesa Switch<br>county: TX: Dawson<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: OSM Oncor 'Lamesa Substation' 1.2 mi NW of the SH 349 x US 87 junction, matching the notice.<br>source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/300613691]]></description><Point><coordinates>-101.9384,32.7193</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Border Switch</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: oncor-border-to-quarry-field<br>project: Border to Quarry Field<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 6<br>window: Late<br>substation: Border Switch<br>county: TX: Loving<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Planned switch not in OSM; placed ~6 mi south of the TX-NM line (32.000) and ~9 mi north of Quarry Field per Oncor; consistent with '7 mi SE of RM 652 &amp; CR 300' (OSM RM 652 passes ~31.985,-103.73).<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/dam/oncorwww/documents/about-us/transmission-system/current-trasmission-line-projects/border-switch-to-clearfork-switch/Border-Clearfork%20QA%20Handout%20(Jan%2015-2025).docx_safe.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-103.64,31.913</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Quarry Field Switch</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: oncor-border-to-quarry-field<br>project: Border to Quarry Field<br>kv: 345<br>stage: 6<br>window: Late<br>substation: Quarry Field Switch<br>county: TX: Loving<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: OSM 'Quarry Field Switching Station' (Oncor, 345/138 kV).<br>source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1006404970]]></description><Point><coordinates>-103.6381,31.7831</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Drill Hole Switch</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[proje