: approx<br>how_placed: Offset ~1 mi ESE of Redland Switch per Oncor (line length 1.63-1.78 mi); Longleaf Power Station not in OSM.<br>source: https://www.oncor.com/content/oncorwww/us/en/home/about-us/transmission-systems/current-transmission-line-projects/REDLAND_LONGLEAF_345_kV_TRANSMISSION_LINE_PROJECT.html]]></description><Point><coordinates>-94.663,31.414</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Joshua Falls Substation (Appalachian Power; to be relocated ~2 mi SE)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: valley-link<br>project: Valley Link<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Joshua Falls Substation (Appalachian Power; to be relocated ~2 mi SE)<br>county: VA: Campbell<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: HIFLD substation layer point named JOSHUA FALLS (765 kV, Campbell Co.) for the existing station; Appalachian Power plans to relocate it about 2 miles southeast, and the new site is not geocoded.<br>source: https://www.aeptransmission.com/virginia/JoshuaFallsStation]]></description><Point><coordinates>-79.0362,37.4254</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Yeat Substation (proposed, Dominion/Valley Link)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: valley-link<br>project: Valley Link<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Yeat Substation (proposed, Dominion/Valley Link)<br>county: VA: Culpeper<br>location_quality: town<br>how_placed: Culpeper County resolution places it in the Richardsville area of SE Culpeper County; point is the Richardsville hamlet (Nominatim).<br>source: https://web.culpepercounty.gov/community/page/immediate-press-release-4172026]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.7289,38.4001</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Amos Substation (John E. Amos plant, AEP)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: valley-link<br>project: Valley Link<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Amos Substation (John E. Amos plant, AEP)<br>county: WV: Putnam<br>location_quality: exact<br>how_placed: HIFLD substation layer point named JOHN AMOS (765 kV, Putnam Co.).<br>source: https://vltransmission.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/ValleyNorth_AnnouncementPackage_WV-1.pdf]]></description><Point><coordinates>-81.8294,38.4737</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Welton Spring(s) Substation (proposed)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: valley-link<br>project: Valley Link<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Welton Spring(s) Substation (proposed)<br>county: WV: Hardy<br>location_quality: town<br>how_placed: PJM: 'northwestern Hardy County'; opposition group says the purchased site is on US 220 south of Reynolds Gap Rd. Placed on the US 220 corridor south of Moorefield toward the Grant County line; the exact site is unknown, so allow ~5 mi of error.<br>source: https://stopmarlvirginia.com/welton-springs-substation]]></description><Point><coordinates>-79.03,39.03</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rocky Point Substation (proposed)</name><styleUrl>#sub</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[project_id: valley-link<br>project: Valley Link<br>kv: 765<br>stage: 3<br>window: Open now<br>substation: Rocky Point Substation (proposed)<br>county: MD: Frederick<br>location_quality: approx<br>how_placed: Described as about 2 mi south of the Doubs substation (HIFLD 39.2964,-77.5148) on Potomac Edison land behind the Rocky Point Creamery (OSM 39.2744,-77.5155), near Point of Rocks.<br>source: https://stopmarlvirginia.com/rocky-point-substation]]></description><Point><coordinates>-77.515,39.268</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Study-area counties</name><Placemark><name>Hillje to Blu Lacy</name><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[id: hillje-blu-lacy<br>name: Hillje to Blu Lacy<br>kv: 765<br>utility: CenterPoint and AEP Texas<br>stage: 3<br>stage_label: Open houses / project page<